verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ#They gave me also gall for my meat;¦layout ‚¤textÙ/And in my thirst they gave me vinegar to drink.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse…¤book§chapterE«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses—„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines“‚¤textÙ+Let their table become a snare before them:¦layout ‚¤textÙ2And that which should have been for their welfare,¦layout§quote_1‚¤textµlet it become a trap.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ.Let their eyes be darkened, that they see not;¦layout ‚¤textÙ*And make their loins continually to shake.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ%Pour out thine indignation upon them,¦layout ‚¤textÙ-And let thy wrathful anger take hold of them.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ!Let their habitation be desolate;¦layout ‚¤textÙ"And let none dwell in their tents.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ.For they persecute him whom thou hast smitten;¦layout ‚¤textÙ;And they talk to the grief of those whom thou hast wounded.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ!Add iniquity unto their iniquity:¦layout ‚¤textÙ-And let them not come into thy righteousness.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ2Let them be blotted out of the book of the living,¦layout ‚¤textÙ&And not be written with the righteous.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse…¤book§chapterE«first_verseªlast_verse!¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤text¼But I am poor and sorrowful:¦layout ‚¤textÙ,Let thy salvation, O God, set me up on high.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ*I will praise the name of God with a song,¦layout ‚¤textÙ'And will magnify him with thanksgiving.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤text¿This also shall please the LORD¦layout ‚¤textÙ7Better than an ox or bullock that hath horns and hoofs.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÃ¥li